1
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:11,200
JUJUTSU KAISEN

2
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:38,690
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

3
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:32,990
Episode 57
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 4

4
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:41,340
The rules' idea of continuation is
just a cover for the real plan.

5
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:43,030
Mark my words.

6
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,700
When only the strong remain,

7
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:47,920
Kenjaku is going to drop
a bomb on the game,

8
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:51,130
and the Culling Game
will fulfill its purpose.

9
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:55,320
I don't know what kind of bomb
Kenjaku's going to drop.

10
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,810
But it's going to happen
in the near future.

11
00:01:58,810 --> 00:02:01,120
Maybe even this very moment.

12
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:05,340
That's why I'm preparing by
gathering strong allies

13
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,320
and stocking up points.

14
00:02:07,990 --> 00:02:09,740
I have a few questions.

15
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:13,500
I doubt she's that strong.

16
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:18,360
That woman is bait to lure other Players
here for whatever reason works.

17
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:21,260
People tend to be less wary
of women, you know.

18
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:23,410
And when you're done using her,

19
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:25,620
you can just kill her
for her points, right?

20
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,880
What are you talking about?

21
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,800
I'd never do that.

22
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:34,870
Reggie-sama is my true knight!

23
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:38,140
So long as I serve him, he'll protect me!

24
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,270
How naïve and stupid.

25
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:44,380
Do you and your allies possess at
least 100 points between all of you?

26
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:47,190
Well, yeah.

27
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,580
A new rule will be added soon.

28
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:53,210
It'll let Players transfer
points between each other.

29
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:58,320
Hand over all of your points.

30
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,950
Negotiations have broken down.

31
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:06,890
He vanished?!

32
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,640
Hey!

33
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,050
Nue!

34
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,710
Whoa!

35
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:15,980
Hey!

36
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,720
Don't let me see your face again.

37
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:26,510
Oh. I get it, I get it.

38
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:30,470
I thought you were being lax,
but you can't kill us, can you?

39
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:33,630
You want the points we
possess, after all.

40
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:34,960
But...

41
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,210
if you don't fight to kill,

42
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:40,960
you'll regret it once you're dead.

43
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:06,740
Hey!

44
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:08,820
I'm down here, too!

45
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:10,730
Iori Hazenoki, Current Points: 35

46
00:04:09,350 --> 00:04:10,450
He dead?

47
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,400
You're okay with this?!

48
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:24,290
This smell!

49
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,550
Is it over?

50
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:40,930
Reggie Star, Current Points: 41

51
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,680
Not yet.

52
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:46,980
He ran into a room before the
explosion, just like you.

53
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:50,270
Not bad.

54
00:04:50,270 --> 00:04:53,100
But you wore him down a good deal, yeah?

55
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,270
Now you get it, right?

56
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:05,860
They have no intention of protecting you.

57
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:11,390
So if you understand that, then get lost.

58
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:20,790
Give it a rest already.

59
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:24,830
Then say it.

60
00:05:26,010 --> 00:05:28,670
Reggie-sama said it for me!

61
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,680
He said he'd protect me!

62
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,790
He said he liked me!

63
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:34,530
So you say it!

64
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,820
Sometimes you run into them—

65
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:45,060
scumbags like you who are all talk

66
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:48,650
and no real action.

67
00:05:48,650 --> 00:05:50,970
Thanks for that throw,

68
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:54,060
but now you're all battered.

69
00:05:53,790 --> 00:05:58,380
Chizuru Hari, Current Points: 28

70
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:56,980
It wasn't easy climbing
all the way back up here.

71
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:59,420
Use the stairs, Neanderthal.

72
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:02,720
Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong,
ding-dong, ding-dong!

73
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:07,510
A Player has added a new
rule to the Culling Game!

74
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:07,870
9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:
name, points, number of
rules added, current Colony.

75
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:14,020
Rule 10: Players are able to
transfer a number of points
of their choosing to other Players.

76
00:06:08,490 --> 00:06:12,670
Rule 10: Players are able to
transfer a number of points

77
00:06:12,670 --> 00:06:14,800
of their choosing to other Players.

78
00:06:15,170 --> 00:06:17,800
What kind of rule is that?

79
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:52,060
Max Elephant!

80
00:06:54,770 --> 00:06:56,640
He did it again?!

81
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,680
You bastard! How dare you...

82
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:21,730
What am I doing?

83
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:25,260
I'll need more points in the future, too.

84
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:29,030
But Tsumiki won't be forced to
participate in the killing anymore.

85
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:30,630
Don't lose your patience.

86
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:32,380
Believe in the others.

87
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:34,630
Don't obsess over these guys' points.

88
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,010
All I need to do

89
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:40,000
is use my full might to brush
away any sparks that fall on me.

90
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:43,130
You have earned five points.

91
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:46,950
Man, what a waste of points.

92
00:07:46,950 --> 00:07:50,720
How pathetic, getting killed before
he could even use his technique.

93
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,530
Did Remi drop out?

94
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:56,720
Even so, it's still two on one.

95
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:59,860
Damn it, I'm still feeling
that first explosion.

96
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,260
Fleeing is not an option!

97
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,000
Maybe I should use my domain?

98
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:09,060
But my domain is still incomplete,

99
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:12,100
so I can't close the barrier
and trap my foe inside.

100
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:17,440
The worst outcome would be them
running off and making me waste it.

101
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:23,690
Look out!

102
00:08:23,690 --> 00:08:25,540
...out!

103
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,900
...out!

104
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,780
...out!

105
00:08:32,570 --> 00:08:34,260
Two on one.

106
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:38,570
Do you really think that's a fair

107
00:08:39,210 --> 00:08:40,910
arrangement?

108
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:45,270
Do you know what they
call people like you?

109
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:49,120
That's right! Cowards!

110
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,990
And cowardly attacks won't work on me!

111
00:08:52,310 --> 00:08:53,570
Behold!

112
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:58,950
Zero damage!

113
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:42,970
JUJUTSU KAISEN

114
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:45,980
JUJUTSU KAISEN

115
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:49,360
Fumihiko Takaba, Current Points: 0

116
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,360
Young boy! I'll help you.

117
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,250
I'm 35 this year,

118
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:54,980
so one look at someone's face and I can
tell if they're a good or bad per—

119
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:58,460
What?

120
00:09:58,850 --> 00:10:02,220
You've got quite a bad look to you!

121
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,770
Whatever!

122
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,500
I use a relative grading scale!
Just like schools!

123
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:09,250
Schools use absolute grading scales.

124
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:11,570
He did protect me.

125
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:14,030
So I can trust him for now, right?

126
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:17,390
What do you make of that, Hazenoki?

127
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:18,690
I don't know him.

128
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:20,490
It's faster to just ask.

129
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:21,560
Hey!

130
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,950
Which type are you?

131
00:10:29,190 --> 00:10:30,900
I get it!

132
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,950
You're asking me

133
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:35,030
if I'm funny

134
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,910
or not,

135
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:38,730
aren't you?

136
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:42,290
I'm not. I'm asking what era—

137
00:10:42,290 --> 00:10:44,240
This costume I'm wearing

138
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:46,430
is modeled after the hero

139
00:10:46,430 --> 00:10:49,900
who first made me laugh my guts out!

140
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,780
So to honor this costume,

141
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:54,040
I can't let my jokes fall flat!

142
00:10:54,420 --> 00:11:00,380
Here's a gag I just thought of.
Try using it on your sweetheart.

143
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:00,890
Curse

144
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,510
Be ready for something!

145
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,650
Curse

146
00:11:12,090 --> 00:11:14,890
"I don't want you as my Wi-Fi!"

147
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,790
What a shitty audience!

148
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:28,520
There are always jerks like you!

149
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:31,670
People who forgot how
to laugh in the womb,

150
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:34,700
and yet always sit at
the front of the venue!

151
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,540
You might be the problem.

152
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:38,000
Yet even so!

153
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,440
He has the same vibes.

154
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,120
I won't abandon you, either!

155
00:11:42,090 --> 00:11:44,030
Because I'm

156
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:47,890
an entertainer!

157
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,610
He's fast!

158
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:57,320
His cursed energy skyrocketed!

159
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:59,560
The shift in output is massive!

160
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,490
This guy is strong!

161
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:02,830
Be careful.

162
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:08,050
I'm an old-school entertainer
who's pro-violence!

163
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:10,830
Now, what will you do,

164
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:11,710
young boy?!

165
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:19,010
We'll split those two up.

166
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:22,900
That other sorcerer is likely capable
of turning his body parts into bombs.

167
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:25,560
And he's using the reverse
cursed technique to—

168
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:27,270
You're too close!

169
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,490
Kogane!

170
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,800
Yes?

171
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:32,350
Pull up Hiromi Higuruma's information.

172
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:35,150
Itadori's the one who added that rule.

173
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,150
Search Results

174
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,150
Hiromi Higuruma

175
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,150
Points

176
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,150
Rule Added

177
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,150
Current Colony: Tokyo No. 1

178
00:12:35,150 --> 00:12:36,900
Points

179
00:12:37,250 --> 00:12:39,880
I'm done with this Colony.

180
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,660
If you'll back down, I'll let you go.

181
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:47,290
Huh?! Where do you think you stand?!

182
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:51,280
I need to recover the points
I lost from you killing Hari!

183
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,410
Hey, you.

184
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:53,650
It's Takaba!

185
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:57,760
If you're going to kill
that bomb bastard,

186
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,320
then if you can,

187
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,710
try to steal his points first.

188
00:13:03,230 --> 00:13:04,710
Okay, young boy.

189
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,300
I accept your request.

190
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:14,600
But I'm an entertainer.

191
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:18,600
I'll never do anything that would rob
a person of their ability to smile.

192
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,900
As long as you win, I don't care.

193
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:30,790
Curse

194
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:30,790
Sparking!

195
00:13:36,310 --> 00:13:38,090
What a dangerous technique!

196
00:13:38,410 --> 00:13:39,210
Bam!

197
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:40,440
Time for fireworks!

198
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,470
However,

199
00:13:42,470 --> 00:13:44,670
in variety shows...

200
00:13:49,530 --> 00:13:50,580
He's gone?!

201
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:54,570
Red is banned.

202
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,970
Don't make light of m—

203
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,720
I'm glad you aren't my enemy, Takaba.

204
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:13,450
Now there's a line I've
always wanted to hear!

205
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:16,210
Later, young boy!

206
00:14:16,210 --> 00:14:17,420
Don't die.

207
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,190
Aw.

208
00:14:20,190 --> 00:14:22,240
That guy's dead now.

209
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:25,930
After that much mockery,
Hazenoki will get serious.

210
00:14:25,930 --> 00:14:28,020
Worry about yourself.

211
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:29,190
I told you, didn't I?

212
00:14:29,190 --> 00:14:32,180
I've already achieved my
objective in this Colony.

213
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:35,940
So now I can fight for real.
I won't hold back.

214
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,560
Max Elephant!

215
00:15:23,970 --> 00:15:26,570
You even have one like that?!

216
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:54,990
You've figured out my
technique, haven't you?

217
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:58,210
But a water attack is pretty
simplistic, isn't it?

218
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:06,170
You manifest what's on those receipts,

219
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:08,320
but that's not exactly right, is it?

220
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:10,290
You're right.

221
00:17:10,290 --> 00:17:15,110
It's hard to describe, but I'd
call it reenacting contracts.

222
00:17:15,110 --> 00:17:17,970
For example, I can do this, too.

223
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:20,870
Contractual Re-Creation.

224
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,730
What I just used

225
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:32,070
was a receipt for a two-night, three-day
stay at the 5-star ryokan, Hoshizoratei,

226
00:17:32,070 --> 00:17:34,360
complete with oil treatment.

227
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:39,330
In other words, my body is now
as refreshed as it would be

228
00:17:39,330 --> 00:17:44,160
after resting up and relaxing
in a hot spring for two days.

229
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,880
Now, how are you faring in comparison?

230
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:49,060
You have injuries from our earlier fight,

231
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,460
and you've employed multiple
shikigami at once.

232
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:53,510
You must be exhausted.

233
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:56,320
I often employ multiple
shikigami at once.

234
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:58,090
The problem is that

235
00:17:58,090 --> 00:18:01,440
one of those was Max Elephant,
which I usually use alone.

236
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:06,580
You can readily draw out and
dismiss your shikigami,

237
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:10,450
but that's not true once
they're injured, is it?

238
00:18:10,450 --> 00:18:14,080
That's why you won't pull out your dog
that can run, attack, and defend.

239
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,200
Because of that,

240
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:19,240
you've been forced to use multiple
one-trick shikigami at once.

241
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:23,790
It's a battle of attrition where neither
of us can use big, high-output moves.

242
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:25,350
It's futile, see?

243
00:18:25,350 --> 00:18:27,700
You can't kill me.

244
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:31,090
That's true.

245
00:18:31,090 --> 00:18:32,510
In which case, I'll run.

246
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:33,900
Hold it.

247
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:44,570
It won't be that easy.

248
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:49,900
Mobile Terrace

249
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:51,360
Monday, November 12th

250
00:18:56,290 --> 00:18:58,760
A community gymnasium?

251
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:01,880
Did he flee inside?
Or is he luring me in?

252
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,900
I could smoke him out with fire,

253
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:07,380
but getting into another
chase would be annoying.

254
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:09,790
Well, what shall I do?

255
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,670
Good. It's just as I imagined.

256
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:16,080
This is the perfect size.

257
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:21,510
What do you think you're
planning, you damn brat?

258
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:25,620
You already have something
set up, don't you?

259
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:33,640
All sorcerers tell lies.

260
00:20:29,710 --> 00:20:33,410
The things I recreate are like shikigami,

261
00:20:33,410 --> 00:20:36,630
so I can give them simple commands.

262
00:20:36,630 --> 00:20:39,450
Knives normally don't fly, right?

263
00:20:40,460 --> 00:20:44,520
Given your personality, I think it's
pointless to ask, but I will anyway.

264
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:47,800
If you give me your points,
I'll give you an easy death.

265
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:52,260
Barrier techniques are
difficult, aren't they?

266
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,250
No matter how long I've tried,

267
00:20:55,250 --> 00:20:58,240
I haven't been able to get the hang
of placing an artificial space

268
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:00,530
of different size over reality.

269
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,750
Which is why...

270
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:03,990
No way...

271
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:08,820
I'm using this gymnasium as-is

272
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:11,710
to deploy my domain.

273
00:21:11,710 --> 00:21:13,380
He can use that?

274
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:35,380
Domain Expansion:

275
00:21:35,890 --> 00:21:37,350
Chimera Shadow Garden.

276
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:44,570
Domain Expansion: Chimera Shadow Garden

277
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:47,950
He's a sorcerer on that level?!

278
00:21:48,470 --> 00:21:52,450
I never said I didn't have big moves.

279
00:23:26,110 --> 00:23:29,550
Even if it's incomplete,
a domain is still a domain!

280
00:23:28,890 --> 00:23:31,540
I'm pulling out my trump
card and activating it!

281
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,110
Not yet! Endure a little longer!

282
00:23:33,110 --> 00:23:34,030
I acknowledge your strength.

283
00:23:34,030 --> 00:23:35,940
Which of us will get crushed first?!

284
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:38,430
Get crushed!

285
